---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import '../styles/products.css';

const source = 'https://github.com/frostdev-ops/crosspane';
const guide = `${source}/blob/master/docs/running.md`;
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Crosspane — Your computers. One workspace."
  description="One keyboard and mouse across your Mac and Linux desktop. Bring individual application windows along with Crosspane, an open-source project by Frostdev."
  path="/crosspane"
  image="/projects/crosspane-flow.webp"
>
  <div class="product-page">
    <section class="product-hero" aria-labelledby="crosspane-title">
      <div class="product-intro">
        <p class="product-eyebrow">Across the desk</p>
        <img class="product-logo" src="/projects/crosspane.webp" width="900" height="301" alt="Crosspane" />
        <h1 class="product-title" id="crosspane-title">Your computers.<br />One workspace.</h1>
        <p class="product-lead">One keyboard. One mouse. Your Mac and Linux desktop, working together. Bring an app window to the screen where you need it.</p>
        <div class="product-actions">
          <a class="product-button" href={guide}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="product-button secondary" href={source}>View source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="product-meta">Early development · macOS + Linux / Hyprland · Open source</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="product-hero-art">
        <img src="/projects/crosspane-flow.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Concept illustration of two computers connected by a flowing ribbon of light, with an application window between them." fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption>Two machines. A shared working space. Concept artwork.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="product-section" aria-labelledby="desk-title">
      <div class="product-section-heading">
        <p class="product-eyebrow">Keep your flow</p>
        <h2 id="desk-title">Let the work cross over.</h2>
        <p>Keep each computer’s apps and environment. Choose where you work with them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-grid">
        <article class="product-card">
          <span class="crosspane-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h3>Cross the edge</h3>
          <p>Move your pointer across a touching display edge. Your keyboard and mouse follow to the next machine.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <span class="crosspane-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h3>Bring a window</h3>
          <p>Project a single application window onto another computer. The app keeps running on its original machine.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="product-card">
          <span class="crosspane-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h3>Make the desk yours</h3>
          <p>Arrange displays in Settings to match your desk. Choose modifier remaps and optional text or image clipboard sharing.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-section product-split" aria-labelledby="control-title">
      <div class="product-section-heading">
        <p class="product-eyebrow">You choose the connection</p>
        <h2 id="control-title">Paired directly.<br />Permission by permission.</h2>
        <p>Compare a pairing code on both machines. Then choose what each peer can control, share, browse or present.</p>
        <a class="product-text-link" href={`${guide}#pair-two-machines-once`}>Explore the setup guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="product-panel crosspane-control">
        <div>
          <span class="crosspane-status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3>Your machines, connected</h3>
          <p>Peer-to-peer over your LAN, direct Ethernet or Thunderbolt networking, with authenticated connections using TLS 1.3.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Sharing is your choice</h3>
          <p>Clipboard sharing starts off in both directions. Enable only the permissions you want each paired machine to have.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Take control back</h3>
          <p>Release input from the tray or menu bar. Use the panic command to end every session and disarm edge crossing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-section" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <div class="product-section-heading">
        <p class="product-eyebrow">Start with two machines</p>
        <h2 id="start-title">A Mac. A Hyprland desktop. Your desk.</h2>
        <p>Crosspane is in early development. The running guide covers source builds, signing, permissions and platform-specific limits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-split">
        <article class="product-panel">
          <p class="product-eyebrow">Current platform scope</p>
          <h3>macOS + Linux</h3>
          <p>Apple Silicon with macOS 26+ is the Mac target. Hyprland is the current Linux backend.</p>
          <p class="product-caption">Windows, GNOME and KDE are planned. Mac window projection mirrors the source by default.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="product-panel">
          <p class="product-eyebrow">Get connected</p>
          <h3>Build. Pair. Arrange.</h3>
          <p>Install on both machines, compare the pairing code, then place your displays in Settings and enable input control.</p>
          <p class="product-caption">Use the window picker to bring an app over. The source machine must grant permission to browse its windows.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="product-cta" aria-labelledby="try-title">
      <p class="product-eyebrow">More room for your work</p>
      <h2 id="try-title">Make the whole desk yours.</h2>
      <p>Explore the current build, or follow what comes next.</p>
      <div class="product-actions">
        <a class="product-button" href={guide}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="product-button secondary" href={`${source}/blob/master/docs/wp/README.md`}>Follow development <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .crosspane-number { display: block; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; color: var(--product-accent, #8de0ee); font-size: 0.75rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  .crosspane-control > div + div { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgb(143 168 192 / 0.2); }
  .crosspane-status { display: block; width: 0.5rem; height: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; background: var(--product-accent, #8de0ee); border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: 0 0 1rem rgb(141 224 238 / 0.25); }
</style>
